name: sim.ruckigStep
description: Executes a call to the Ruckig online trajectory generator. The Ruckig online trajectory generator provides instantaneous trajectory generation capabilities for motion control systems. This function steps forward a trajectory generation algorithm previously prepared via sim.ruckigPos or sim.ruckigVel
luaSynopsis: int result, list newPosVelAccel, float synchronizationTime = sim.ruckigStep(int handle, float cycleTime)
pythonSynopsis: int result, float[] newPosVelAccel, float synchronizationTime = sim.ruckigStep(int handle, float cycleTime)
inputs:
1. handle: handle of the object created via sim.ruckigPos or sim.ruckigVel.
2. cycleTime: cycle time or simulation step. Should always be a multiple of the base cycle time
outputs:
1. result: return value of the update function in the motion library:
    - 1: Result::Finished (final state reached)
    - 0: Result::Working (final state not yet reached)
    - -100: Result::ErrorInvalidInput
    - -101: Result::ErrorTrajectoryDuration
    - -110: Result::ErrorExecutionTimeCalculation
    - -111: Result::ErrorSynchronizationCalculation
2. newPosVelAccel: new positions, velocities and accelerations, i.e. [p0 ... pn v0 ... vn a0 ... an]
replacedBy:
- name: step, class: RuckigPosition, file: RuckigPosition_step.method
- name: data, class: RuckigPosition, file: RuckigPosition_data.method
- name: step, class: RuckigVelocity, file: RuckigVelocity_step.method
- name: data, class: RuckigVelocity, file: RuckigVelocity_data.method
